WEBVTT

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:08.080
Bye, bye!

00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:11.620
See ya! Now then...

00:00:13.830 --> 00:00:14.250
"Hina"

00:00:14.250 --> 00:00:15.750
"Hina"
I'm gonna head over to the club room!

00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:16.450
I'm gonna head over to the club room!

00:00:16.450 --> 00:00:18.950
Well, she's sure motivated.

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:09.450
Jeez, you're so late!
Let's hurry up and go fishing for whiting.

00:02:09.450 --> 00:02:11.790
Well, ya seem rarin' to go.

00:02:11.790 --> 00:02:14.160
Did you figure out a good way to catch them?

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:16.750
Yeah! I've got it down!

00:02:16.750 --> 00:02:19.750
So let's go already!

00:02:19.750 --> 00:02:22.120
Yeah, she's hooked...

00:02:27.250 --> 00:02:29.540
There's a reason I couldn't
catch any yesterday...

00:02:29.540 --> 00:02:34.330
That's because there's one huge difference
between live bait and artificial bait.

00:02:34.330 --> 00:02:39.950
And that difference is...
Will you move or will you not move?

00:02:39.950 --> 00:02:42.200
Who exactly are ya talkin' to?

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:45.080
Whiting respond to things that move!

00:02:45.080 --> 00:02:50.660
With live bait, they'll usually move
on their own still, attracting the fish.

00:02:50.660 --> 00:02:53.500
But artificial bait will not move.

00:02:53.500 --> 00:02:56.950
Yesterday, I used the same length
as live bait and on top of that,

00:02:56.950 --> 00:02:59.910
I didn't move my rig. Which obviously
means the bait didn't move,

00:02:59.910 --> 00:03:03.000
and the whiting lost interest.

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:05.370
"Yesterday was about to here"
So today, I'm going to make
the artificial bait a little longer

00:03:05.370 --> 00:03:06.200
So today, I'm going to make
the artificial bait a little longer

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:12.950
and continuously move my rig around
to strike the interest of the whiting.

00:03:12.950 --> 00:03:15.120
That's the method I'm going to use today.

00:03:16.750 --> 00:03:21.290
I mean... that's all written right here.

00:03:21.290 --> 00:03:23.750
Right, then. Go for it, Tsurugi.

00:03:23.750 --> 00:03:25.500
By myself?!

00:03:25.500 --> 00:03:28.620
Ya gotta be the one to catch the first one.

00:03:28.620 --> 00:03:31.080
O-Okay.

00:03:33.620 --> 00:03:35.750
Go!

00:03:53.290 --> 00:03:56.540
S-See? I already felt a wiggle on the first try!

00:03:56.540 --> 00:03:58.540
Wow, you're already showing results.

00:03:58.540 --> 00:04:00.870
Ya might catch one already.

00:04:02.040 --> 00:04:05.200
I need to make sure I keep moving the rig.

00:04:07.450 --> 00:04:08.580
Again!

00:04:08.580 --> 00:04:14.000
This wiggle and tug... i-is pretty fun.

00:04:16.500 --> 00:04:18.830
If this is already happening on my first try...

00:04:20.200 --> 00:04:22.250
I can do this!

00:04:37.450 --> 00:04:39.370
I'm not done yet!

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:49.000
Hi-yah!

00:04:57.910 --> 00:05:00.330
She's gettin' close, but not catching any yet.

00:05:00.330 --> 00:05:01.870
Yes...

00:05:01.870 --> 00:05:04.540
There, there, there, there...

00:05:04.540 --> 00:05:07.200
She's almost got it.

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:09.160
Shake!

00:05:09.160 --> 00:05:14.250
That's a good boy. Who's a good boy?
It's you. Yes, you are...

00:05:14.250 --> 00:05:19.540
She's moving from point to point
to find a more active school of fish.

00:05:19.540 --> 00:05:23.870
So run and gun... Looks like
she looked up a few things.

00:05:23.870 --> 00:05:26.290
See you later!

00:05:43.080 --> 00:05:45.910
I'm getting hits, but I haven't caught one yet.

00:05:45.910 --> 00:05:50.160
It looked so much easier
online and in the videos.

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:53.120
Maybe I'm just...

00:05:56.410 --> 00:05:58.660
Here. Have some barley tea.

00:05:58.660 --> 00:06:01.370
Th-Thank you.

00:06:01.370 --> 00:06:02.910
You've been fishing nonstop.

00:06:02.910 --> 00:06:05.870
You should take a break
or you're gonna get heatstroke.

00:06:05.870 --> 00:06:09.870
Yeah. I seem to forget
about time when I'm fishing.

00:06:09.870 --> 00:06:11.830
I know, right?

00:06:11.830 --> 00:06:14.290
Seems like you're having
a hard time catching any.

00:06:15.410 --> 00:06:18.040
I keep getting bites though...

00:06:18.040 --> 00:06:19.450
I wonder why.

00:06:19.450 --> 00:06:21.950
Are you following everything you saw online?

00:06:21.950 --> 00:06:25.000
Yeah. I found a video where
they were fishing the same way,

00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:27.160
so I'm trying to follow that but...

00:06:27.160 --> 00:06:28.750
I'm not catching any.

00:06:28.750 --> 00:06:30.870
I see.

00:06:30.870 --> 00:06:34.000
Don't worry. You'll eventually catch one.

00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:36.910
Maybe the fish are just in a bad mood today.

00:06:36.910 --> 00:06:39.080
Fish have moods?

00:06:39.080 --> 00:06:41.910
There are days you can't
go on if you don't think that.

00:06:41.910 --> 00:06:44.040
I see. That's a good point.

00:06:44.040 --> 00:06:47.450
Not to mention, you're not fishing
in the same spot as the video.

00:06:47.450 --> 00:06:50.580
If you're fishing in different parts of
the sea, the whiting will act different,

00:06:50.580 --> 00:06:52.620
so don't let it get to you.

00:06:53.950 --> 00:06:56.500
I see... So it is different.

00:06:56.500 --> 00:06:58.080
What's up?

00:06:59.540 --> 00:07:04.540
If I'm not catching any, that must
mean there's something different.

00:07:04.540 --> 00:07:09.950
I was just copying what I was seeing.
I haven't made any tweaks.

00:07:09.950 --> 00:07:13.080
There has to be something
different from the video...

00:07:13.080 --> 00:07:15.120
Something different...

00:07:15.120 --> 00:07:16.040
"Catching Whiting with Hyper Isome"

00:07:16.040 --> 00:07:20.040
"Catching Whiting with Hyper Isome"
Come to think of it, all the
whiting in the video were big.

00:07:20.040 --> 00:07:22.160
They were all big and over 20 centimeters.
They didn't catch any small ones.

00:07:22.160 --> 00:07:25.080
"Catching lots of excellent whiting"
They were all big and over 20 centimeters.
They didn't catch any small ones.

00:07:25.080 --> 00:07:25.620
They were all big and over 20 centimeters.
They didn't catch any small ones.

00:07:25.620 --> 00:07:30.450
Natsumi, how big were the
whiting you caught yesterday?

00:07:30.450 --> 00:07:36.080
I'd say about 15 centimeters.
They're all pretty small this time of year.

00:07:37.370 --> 00:07:42.700
The length of my bait is about
the same as the video. Maybe...

00:07:42.700 --> 00:07:45.910
If I cut off the thicker end and reattach it...

00:07:49.330 --> 00:07:51.450
Did you make it just a little shorter?

00:07:51.450 --> 00:07:55.500
Yeah. I didn't want it to be any
less appealing, so just a little.

00:07:55.500 --> 00:07:57.040
I think the artificial bait was too long

00:07:57.040 --> 00:08:00.000
and the hook wasn't reaching their mouths.

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:03.870
I see. That's a good thought.

00:08:03.870 --> 00:08:07.500
I wouldn't have thought of it
if it wasn't for you. Thank you.

00:08:08.660 --> 00:08:12.120
I-I didn't really do anything...

00:08:12.120 --> 00:08:14.290
What? Are you embarrassed?

00:08:14.290 --> 00:08:15.870
Shut up!

00:08:15.870 --> 00:08:19.330
Okay. If I can't catch one
after this, I give up!

00:08:19.330 --> 00:08:22.200
It just means the whiting
were in a bad mood today.

00:08:22.200 --> 00:08:23.200
You've got this.

00:08:23.200 --> 00:08:25.370
Go get them!

00:08:28.330 --> 00:08:30.750
Hi-yah!

00:08:45.660 --> 00:08:48.500
There! They're following it!

00:08:48.500 --> 00:08:53.370
I think I'll reel in my line a bit
slower so they can latch on...

00:08:53.370 --> 00:08:57.580
Without stopping. Slowly, slowly...

00:09:04.250 --> 00:09:05.950
There!

00:09:07.120 --> 00:09:11.540
D-Don't panic. Slowly reel them in...

00:09:31.950 --> 00:09:35.700
I-I caught a whiting!

00:09:36.950 --> 00:09:39.250
You did it!

00:09:41.410 --> 00:09:44.870
I did it!

00:09:44.870 --> 00:09:48.370
I really did it!

00:09:54.830 --> 00:09:56.700
This looks yummy!

00:09:56.700 --> 00:09:59.250
Let's eat!

00:10:05.410 --> 00:10:07.370
But I'm surprised you figured it out.

00:10:07.370 --> 00:10:10.830
You just shortened the bait
a bit and we caught this many.

00:10:10.830 --> 00:10:12.790
Heh.

00:10:12.790 --> 00:10:15.910
Wasn't it fun figurin' stuff out
on yer own and fishin'?

00:10:15.910 --> 00:10:18.660
Yes! It almost made me cry!

00:10:18.660 --> 00:10:24.080
Figuring stuff out and learnin'
from it is its own reward.

00:10:24.080 --> 00:10:28.870
Keep tryin' different things to
figure out yer own way of fishin'.

00:10:28.870 --> 00:10:32.700
You actually say decent
things at times, President.

00:10:34.830 --> 00:10:38.620
There's still plenty of artificial bait left,
so let's come back tomorrow.

00:10:38.620 --> 00:10:42.080
Aw, but we already caught this many. We're good.

00:10:42.080 --> 00:10:43.830
It's hot on the beach.

00:10:43.830 --> 00:10:50.370
Then I'll go myself! I'll figure
out a way to catch even more!

00:10:50.370 --> 00:10:53.000
Yeah, she's completely hooked.

00:10:53.000 --> 00:10:57.950
"Report 12"
"'From Now On...'"
"Even the bones are yummy"

00:11:04.080 --> 00:11:06.910
First comes rock! Rock, paper, scissors!

00:11:18.200 --> 00:11:21.040
Good work. I'll bring you some barley tea.

00:11:21.040 --> 00:11:23.120
Thanks...

00:11:26.000 --> 00:11:31.080
Hina... This is all the barley tea
we have left. Oh, Ohno-<i>senpai</i>.

00:11:31.080 --> 00:11:33.250
It's pretty hot today.

00:11:38.950 --> 00:11:41.870
It cooled down.

00:11:41.870 --> 00:11:44.580
Hup.

00:11:44.580 --> 00:11:48.120
I guess we do drink a lot
more when it gets hotter.

00:11:48.120 --> 00:11:50.790
Let's make a lot in advance.

00:11:50.790 --> 00:11:53.870
It'd be awful if we ran out
when we really need it.

00:11:53.870 --> 00:11:57.580
It's sort of a waste of money to
always go buy it at the vending machines.

00:11:59.120 --> 00:12:00.500
Barley tea is the best.

00:12:00.500 --> 00:12:02.500
Thank you, barley tea.

00:12:02.500 --> 00:12:05.540
It's a good idea to make a lot,

00:12:05.540 --> 00:12:09.330
but I can never remember which one is mine.

00:12:09.330 --> 00:12:10.790
Should we write our names on them?

00:12:10.790 --> 00:12:12.620
Good idea!

00:12:18.000 --> 00:12:21.040
You're matching. How cute.

00:12:21.040 --> 00:12:25.200
Oh, that? That's...

00:12:26.370 --> 00:12:29.450
Hina, how'd you do on your midterms?

00:12:29.450 --> 00:12:32.080
I-I think okay.

00:12:33.580 --> 00:12:34.950
What about you, Natsumi?

00:12:34.950 --> 00:12:37.120
I averaged over 90.

00:12:37.120 --> 00:12:40.290
But you don't look smart at all...

00:12:40.290 --> 00:12:42.410
Are you trying to pick a fight?

00:12:42.410 --> 00:12:47.910
But because of you, my score in math
wasn't as bad I as thought it'd be.

00:12:49.160 --> 00:12:51.700
I'll be counting on you for finals, too.

00:12:51.700 --> 00:12:54.620
Well, if you insist.

00:12:54.620 --> 00:13:00.540
Hey, since our tests are done, remember
what we talked about the other day?

00:13:00.540 --> 00:13:02.660
Making a plushie of a horse mackerel.

00:13:02.660 --> 00:13:05.910
Oh, a felt one? Wanna try?

00:13:05.910 --> 00:13:09.200
Well, sure. Why not?

00:13:09.200 --> 00:13:12.290
Then do you wanna come over right now?

00:13:13.620 --> 00:13:15.290
Sure, let's go.

00:13:15.290 --> 00:13:16.910
I'm gonna change and then I'll head over.

00:13:16.910 --> 00:13:18.620
Sure!

00:13:25.040 --> 00:13:26.700
Hello.

00:13:26.700 --> 00:13:31.330
Coming! Oh? Is that you, Natsumi?

00:13:31.330 --> 00:13:34.200
It is. It's been a while.

00:13:34.200 --> 00:13:36.950
Wow, you've gotten so big!

00:13:36.950 --> 00:13:41.000
I heard that you're in that
fishing... club with Hina, too.

00:13:41.000 --> 00:13:43.620
Yes. It's called the Breakwater Club.

00:13:43.620 --> 00:13:45.750
My daughter is awful at sports,

00:13:45.750 --> 00:13:48.080
so I've been terrified that
she might fall into the ocean.

00:13:48.080 --> 00:13:50.700
I hope you'll keep your eye on her, Natsumi.

00:13:50.700 --> 00:13:54.120
Leave it to me. I'm an awesome swimmer.

00:13:54.120 --> 00:13:57.200
And we have some training coming up
where we swim with our clothes on.

00:13:57.200 --> 00:13:58.700
Oh, really?

00:13:58.700 --> 00:14:02.540
Hina can only dog paddle,
so I'm counting on you.

00:14:02.540 --> 00:14:02.950
--Sure.

00:14:02.950 --> 00:14:04.250
--Mom!
--Sure.

00:14:04.250 --> 00:14:09.330
You don't need to say any of those things!
Natsumi, hurry up and come up!

00:14:09.330 --> 00:14:12.450
Thanks for letting me come over.

00:14:12.450 --> 00:14:14.950
I hope you'll have dinner with us.

00:14:14.950 --> 00:14:17.200
Thank you.

00:14:18.250 --> 00:14:19.580
What's goin' on?

00:14:19.580 --> 00:14:21.370
Hina's friend's over.

00:14:21.370 --> 00:14:25.160
You know, Natsumi that used to come
over all the time when she was little.

00:14:25.160 --> 00:14:28.330
Oh, her.

00:14:28.330 --> 00:14:32.250
I see. So they're still friends.

00:14:32.250 --> 00:14:34.790
I'm so happy for her.

00:14:34.790 --> 00:14:37.750
I think we can relax now
that she's made some friends.

00:14:37.750 --> 00:14:38.870
Yeah...

00:14:38.870 --> 00:14:41.290
Time for some coffee...

00:14:41.290 --> 00:14:46.370
Natsumi's joining us for dinner,
so make sure you wash up a bit.

00:14:46.370 --> 00:14:49.290
I'll go shave.

00:14:49.290 --> 00:14:53.540
Don't worry about the mess.

00:14:53.540 --> 00:14:55.500
Let's see...

00:14:55.500 --> 00:14:58.580
Whoa...

00:14:58.580 --> 00:15:02.200
Wait, did you make all of these, Hina?

00:15:02.200 --> 00:15:03.540
Yup.

00:15:03.540 --> 00:15:06.580
I guess you really are interested in this stuff.

00:15:06.580 --> 00:15:07.700
Did you make this, too?

00:15:07.700 --> 00:15:10.870
Yup. This is basically my only talent.

00:15:13.580 --> 00:15:16.750
You don't have any games? Wait...

00:15:17.950 --> 00:15:19.410
You don't even have a TV.

00:15:19.410 --> 00:15:21.500
Well, I don't play any games.

00:15:21.500 --> 00:15:24.290
Aw, that's no fun.

00:15:24.290 --> 00:15:27.000
Why did you come over again?

00:15:27.000 --> 00:15:28.250
What did you want to make?

00:15:28.250 --> 00:15:30.580
I think a horse mackerel.

00:15:37.620 --> 00:15:39.200
I cut them!

00:15:43.580 --> 00:15:49.200
We should be doing a blanket stitch,
but whip stitching is the easiest.

00:15:49.200 --> 00:15:51.200
L-Like this?

00:15:52.410 --> 00:15:53.950
Ow!

00:15:53.950 --> 00:15:56.120
Are you okay?

00:15:59.660 --> 00:16:02.500
Next you add in the stuffing...

00:16:02.500 --> 00:16:07.200
And once you sew it all together... you're done!

00:16:07.200 --> 00:16:09.000
I did it!

00:16:09.000 --> 00:16:10.910
All done.

00:16:15.250 --> 00:16:19.540
Y-You did a good job for your first time...

00:16:19.540 --> 00:16:21.750
Hina...

00:16:21.750 --> 00:16:26.370
Here's a gift for you. To thank you
for helping me how to make this.

00:16:26.370 --> 00:16:30.290
You say that, but you just want
to switch with me, don't you?

00:16:30.290 --> 00:16:32.500
Was I that obvious?

00:16:32.500 --> 00:16:35.580
Then, here...

00:16:35.580 --> 00:16:40.080
Here's my gift to you. For helping me study.

00:16:43.790 --> 00:16:46.620
S-Stop staring at it so much.

00:16:46.620 --> 00:16:49.950
W-Well, I'm sure you think I suck anyway.

00:16:49.950 --> 00:16:51.620
I do not!

00:16:51.620 --> 00:16:53.580
Really?

00:16:53.580 --> 00:16:55.540
Dinner's ready!

00:16:55.540 --> 00:16:57.410
Coming!

00:16:59.080 --> 00:17:02.000
Natsumi and I made them.

00:17:02.000 --> 00:17:04.290
That's so nice...

00:17:04.290 --> 00:17:06.580
I want to make one, too.

00:17:09.250 --> 00:17:12.080
Then let's make one! I have plenty of materials!

00:17:12.080 --> 00:17:15.040
When did you...? You had them in the locker?

00:17:15.040 --> 00:17:16.370
Yeah!

00:17:29.540 --> 00:17:31.700
Hey.

00:17:31.700 --> 00:17:33.290
Oh, President.

00:17:33.290 --> 00:17:34.620
Heya.

00:17:34.620 --> 00:17:36.290
Whatcha makin'?

00:17:36.290 --> 00:17:38.080
Felt plushies.

00:17:38.080 --> 00:17:42.160
Hina's super fast at making them,
so it's fun to watch.

00:17:42.160 --> 00:17:44.580
Hina's amazing.

00:17:44.580 --> 00:17:48.000
Huh, that looks pretty fun.

00:17:48.000 --> 00:17:50.080
Would you like to make one, too, President?

00:17:50.080 --> 00:17:53.910
Hina taught me how to make this...

00:17:53.910 --> 00:17:55.330
It's a rockfish.

00:17:55.330 --> 00:17:59.250
Wow you're pretty talented.

00:17:59.250 --> 00:18:02.370
I could make some money off of this.

00:18:02.370 --> 00:18:05.950
I'll pass, though.
Will you make me one, Tsurugi?

00:18:05.950 --> 00:18:08.200
Sure. What would you like?

00:18:08.200 --> 00:18:10.040
An octopus.

00:18:18.750 --> 00:18:19.910
All done!

00:18:19.910 --> 00:18:22.700
Holy crap! You're so fast!

00:18:22.700 --> 00:18:25.040
Is that supposed to be Takohigeya?

00:18:27.950 --> 00:18:29.870
So, hey...

00:18:29.870 --> 00:18:31.830
This might be a weird time
to bring this up, but...

00:18:31.830 --> 00:18:34.660
...are you not interested in the
Handicrafts Club anymore, Hina?

00:18:34.660 --> 00:18:37.500
You look like you're having so
much fun when you make those...

00:18:37.500 --> 00:18:40.790
I figured you still might want to join.

00:18:40.790 --> 00:18:44.160
That really was out of nowhere.
You're the one who bought me the hat,

00:18:44.160 --> 00:18:46.500
making it harder for me to quit, Natsumi!

00:18:46.500 --> 00:18:49.040
Yeah, I guess I was...

00:18:49.040 --> 00:18:51.200
But...

00:18:51.200 --> 00:18:54.700
I can have fun doing handicrafts myself.

00:18:54.700 --> 00:18:59.290
More importantly, I'm having fun
in this club right now, so it's fine.

00:19:01.160 --> 00:19:03.370
Then that's good.

00:19:05.290 --> 00:19:10.910
Actually, even if I wanted to join the
Handicrafts Club, I wouldn't be able to.

00:19:11.870 --> 00:19:12.410
"Handicrafts Club"
"Beginners welcome!!!"

00:19:12.410 --> 00:19:16.660
"Handicrafts Club"
"Beginners welcome!!!"
I decided to peek in just once.

00:19:16.660 --> 00:19:17.160
"Handicrafts Club"
"Beginners welcome!!!"

00:19:23.080 --> 00:19:25.160
What a cute dog.

00:19:25.160 --> 00:19:26.500
That's my dog!

00:19:26.500 --> 00:19:29.160
President, look at my cat, too.

00:19:29.160 --> 00:19:32.500
That's some great stitching.
How did you do that?

00:19:32.500 --> 00:19:34.160
Well...

00:19:34.160 --> 00:19:37.620
There were so many boys there...

00:19:37.620 --> 00:19:41.330
So I gave up...

00:19:41.330 --> 00:19:44.040
I was so scared.

00:19:44.040 --> 00:19:45.290
I see.

00:19:45.290 --> 00:19:49.450
Come to think of it, I guess
our Handicrafts Club is full of guys.

00:19:49.450 --> 00:19:49.950
"She already knew"
Come to think of it, I guess
our Handicrafts Club is full of guys.

00:19:49.950 --> 00:19:50.950
"She already knew"

00:19:56.790 --> 00:19:58.830
All right, let's head on home.

00:19:58.830 --> 00:20:00.500
Okay.

00:20:00.500 --> 00:20:02.410
What should we do with these?

00:20:02.410 --> 00:20:06.580
Should we add magnets
and leave them on the locker?

00:20:06.580 --> 00:20:09.410
Hey, I got an idea.

00:20:09.410 --> 00:20:11.750
Hina, attach a string to this.

00:20:11.750 --> 00:20:13.200
Okay.

00:20:16.700 --> 00:20:21.160
Guess we were the Handicrafts Club today
rather than the Breakwater Club.

00:20:21.160 --> 00:20:23.950
I had a lot of fun.

00:20:23.950 --> 00:20:27.870
I could try the flea market...
or maybe even Takohigeya, or maybe...

00:20:27.870 --> 00:20:31.660
She's definitely got
something up her sleeve again...

00:20:31.660 --> 00:20:34.370
What should we catch tomorrow?

00:20:34.370 --> 00:20:35.830
Whiting!

00:20:35.830 --> 00:20:37.080
Again?

00:20:37.080 --> 00:20:39.660
Well, we have more artificial bait left over.

00:20:39.660 --> 00:20:41.700
And we made plenty of barley tea.

00:20:41.700 --> 00:20:43.830
I'm gonna do my best and
catch a lot again tomorrow!

00:20:43.830 --> 00:20:45.500
Yeah!

00:20:45.500 --> 00:20:46.830
Yeah...

00:20:46.830 --> 00:20:49.370
You sure love whiting.

00:20:49.370 --> 00:20:52.620
"You catch it, you eat it!"

00:20:58.540 --> 00:21:03.250
No fair! You left me out again!

00:21:04.290 --> 00:21:07.120
I should've known this would happen.

00:21:07.120 --> 00:21:11.160
Don't worry! I'll make one for you, too.

00:21:11.160 --> 00:21:13.000
Really?

00:21:13.000 --> 00:21:15.410
Really! I will!

00:21:15.410 --> 00:21:17.540
Um, here you go...

00:21:17.540 --> 00:21:20.450
What would you like her to make for you?

00:21:21.950 --> 00:21:26.120
Well, I am a hunter, so maybe a deer or a boar.

00:21:27.290 --> 00:21:31.660
Uh, we're in the Breakwater Club,
so wouldn't fish be better?

00:21:31.660 --> 00:21:34.330
What kind of fish do you like, Ms. Kotani?

00:21:34.330 --> 00:21:37.160
<i>Chutoro</i>! Oh, and salmon!

00:23:13.160 --> 00:23:15.700
Today's gonna be another hot one.

00:23:15.700 --> 00:23:18.250
I'll bring us some more barley tea.

00:23:19.200 --> 00:23:21.540
Hello!

00:23:21.540 --> 00:23:23.500
Heya!

00:23:24.790 --> 00:23:25.540
President, what should we catch today?

00:23:25.540 --> 00:23:28.830
"Breakwater Club" "Umino High School"
President, what should we catch today?

00:23:28.830 --> 00:23:29.500
"Breakwater Club" "Umino High School"

00:23:30.750 --> 00:23:32.750
Today's Haiku...

00:23:32.750 --> 00:23:34.160
Let's make sure we keep

00:23:34.160 --> 00:23:35.790
the oceans clean and pristine

00:23:35.790 --> 00:23:37.200
for eternity.

00:23:37.200 --> 00:23:39.120
The Breakwater Club.
